# What GitHub's language statistics should reflect: the code written for this
# project, not the libraries and inputs it carries alongside it.
#
# Without these rules the bar reads "Verilog 70%", and that Verilog is
# SkyWater's standard cell library — 2126 of the 2137 .v files in the tree were
# written by somebody else. `linguist-vendored` keeps the files in the
# repository and takes them out of the count.

# The sky130 standard cell library, fetched by tools/fetch_pdk.py from
# google/skywater-pdk-libs-sky130_fd_sc_hd@ac7fb61f, and the same cells as
# open_pdks builds them, fetched by tools/fetch_open_pdks.py.
# `-text` as well as vendored: never convert line endings in content this
# project did not write. tools/common/liberty.py caches the parsed functions
# beside them and stamps the cache with each source's BYTE SIZE, so a CRLF
# checkout silently invalidates all 429 of them -- measured, 65866 -> 68885 on
# the first file. The parsed functions were identical; only the stamp moved.
pdk/**          linguist-vendored
pdk/**          -text

# The puzzle's published material, from janestreet/asic-puzzle-2026. Vendored
# here rather than left as a submodule so this repository stays readable for
# as long as it stands, and not only for as long as the upstream does.
puzzle/**       linguist-vendored
puzzle/**       -text

# Artifacts the pipeline produced: netlists, graphs, solver traces, the review
# packet. Kept because the machine that made them has been sold and they are
# the evidence, but they are output rather than source.
out/**          linguist-generated

# Generated corpus RTL, when a checkout has it. Reproducible from
# tools/stage5_corpus.py, which is the artifact worth reading.
synth/**        linguist-generated
